{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-psqm-wje2-ft2a-lx5i","published":"2026-11-18T20:32:32Z","modified":"2026-11-18T21:45:08.724394582Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-113425"],"summary":"When NGINX Plus or NGINX Open Source is configured as a mail proxy, undisclosed traffic can cause a use-after-free in…","details":"When NGINX Plus or NGINX Open Source is configured as a mail proxy, undisclosed traffic can cause a use-after-free in an nginx worker process. Additionally, attackers can execute code on systems with Address Space Layout Randomization (ASLR) disabled or when the attacker can bypass ASLR.\n\nImpact:\nA remote unauthenticated attacker may crash an nginx worker process or corrupt its memory, disrupting service. Remote code execution is a potential impact. There is no control plane exposure; this is a data plane issue only.\n\n\n\nNote: Software versions which have reached End of Technical Support (EoTS) are not evaluated.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"nginx-mainline","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/nginx-mainline"},"versions":["1.29.8-r0","1.29.8-r1","1.31.2-r0","1.31.2-r1","1.31.2-r2","1.31.3-r2","1.31.3-r3","1.31.4-r4","1.31.5-r4","1.31.6-r4","1.31.7-r4","1.31.8-r4","1.31.8-r5","1.31.9-r5"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-psqm-wje2-ft2a-lx5i.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nginx-stable","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/nginx-stable"},"versions":["1.28.3-r0","1.28.3-r1","1.30.3-r1","1.30.3-r2","1.30.3-r3","1.30.4-r2","1.30.4-r5","1.30.4-r6","1.30.5-r4","1.30.6-r4","1.30.6-r5","1.30.7-r5"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-psqm-wje2-ft2a-lx5i.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nginx","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Alpine:3.24","purl":"pkg:apk/dhi/nginx"},"versions":["1.28.3-r0","1.28.3-r1","1.29.8-r0","1.29